<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Grain, soy basis quietly steady.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Grain, soy basis quietly steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOB grain and soybean bids were steady on Friday in quiet conditions.</p>
<p>Dealers said soybeans continued to be underpinned by a strong export pace. USDA Friday said for the week ended November 7 U.S. net exports of soybeans totaled 1.118 million tonnes, above expectations for 600,000 to 800,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The soybean sales pace for this year was at 12.347 million tonnes, above the year-ago pace of 9.998 million.</p>
<p>Wheat traders continued to await confirmation Pakistan will tender shortly for 200,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat. The tender should be announced in the next few days.</p>
